  note: lap is 4 chunks; the gate fires from chunk 4 on, and the read block is PINNED at 64 columns from there. Against a no-trim accum on the same chain (128 columns) this is 50% of the read cost -- the pair is 'cheaper AND?', never 'equal cost AND?'.
  note: +33.6M buffer parameters, which the optimizer holds two moments for. That is the one axis on which the gated arm is the LARGER of the two, and the reason this gate is not a formality.
  optimizer: MuonWithAuxAdam, 3 groups (57m, 59a, 13a)
  warmup 1/1: loss nan  2.0s  peak 103.35 GiB
  measured: loss nan  1.2s  peak 110.20 GiB

